atrix}.$ \n\nWe proceed to find an orthogonal basis using the Gram-Schmidt process, as follows.\n\n**Step 1**: We set ${v}_{1}={a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n**Step 2**: Next, we find ${v}_{2}$, by using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{2} & ={a}_{2}-\\frac{{a}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{v}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the formula for ${v}_{2}$ in our case gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{2} & ={a}_{2}-\\frac{2\\cdot 1+5\\cdot (-1)+6\\cdot 1}{{1}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{1}^{2}}{v}_{1} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $B=\\{{v}_{1},{v}_{2}\\}=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}\\}$ is an orthogonal basis for $\\text{Col}(A).$\n\nFinally, $b=6,$ $c=5,$ and  \n\n$$\n\\frac{b}{c}=\\frac{6}{5}.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "b145ad9e-f7c2-5436-b124-365beca417e7" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186488306}}] :activity/title "The Gram-Schmidt Process for Two Vectors" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487560}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046658} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186502208} :activity/id #uuid "c6f0a606-7357-5b62-ba3e-c7abaf986519" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050578 :topic/id #uuid "5558fd2c-f6e0-5362-bf8b-7d3500df79a0" :topic/math-academy-id 2127} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186502175 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186414752 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "60d1356a-94ea-5209-96d5-9d9418453443" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414730} {:answer/id #uuid "7ea97cd7-7fc3-5a3d-bc31-abc4a8a14911" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414734} {:answer/id #uuid "7edf9628-a06c-547d-b79b-2b8c3b2e00b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414735} {:answer/id #uuid "a319ab1d-aad5-5d1b-8415-3377cf75bf86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414739} {:answer/id #uuid "d937650c-2bf8-5168-848d-23a4e1590bfc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414743}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186414735} :answer-field/id #uuid "546f2176-ce65-54a2-a805-2b4a861a5018" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414747}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "9ea317f2-12b0-537c-bfd8-c2c151d6c85b" :question/math-academy-id "q-86849" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}a \\\\ b \\\\ c\\end{bmatrix}\\}\n$$\n\nConsider the subspace $\\text{Col}(A)$ and an orthogonal basis $B$ of $\\text{Col}(A),$ where $A$ and $B$ are given above. Given that $B$ is derived from $\\text{Col}(A)$ using the Gram-Schmidt process, what is the value of $\\frac{b}{a}?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that $\\text{Col}(A)$ is the span of the columns of $A.$  \n\nFirst, let's denote\n\n$\\,$ ${a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\\,$ and $\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}.$ \n\nWe proceed to find an orthogonal basis using the Gram-Schmidt process, as follows.\n\n**Step 1**: We set ${v}_{1}={a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n**Step 2**: Next, we find ${v}_{2}$, by using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{2} & ={a}_{2}-\\frac{{a}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{v}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the formula for ${v}_{2}$ in our case gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{2} & ={a}_{2}-\\frac{(-3)\\cdot (-2)+2\\cdot 1+5\\cdot 2}{(-2)^{2}+{1}^{2}+{2}^{2}}{v}_{1} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $B=\\{{v}_{1},{v}_{2}\\}=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\}$ is an orthogonal basis for $\\text{Col}(A).$\n\nFinally, $a=1,$ $b=0,$ and  \n\n$$\n\\frac{b}{a}=\\frac{0}{1}=0.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "3587edc5-deb1-5629-b533-df76f3ade5d0" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186502177}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186502177 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186354526 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "670187cb-2fe0-51db-969e-737152c95412" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352479} {:answer/id #uuid "98365ad9-dec1-5da4-82dc-2689174ee916" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352876} {:answer/id #uuid "ae0603d6-42f1-5fae-9851-950afc52e0b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\sqrt{5}}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353041} {:answer/id #uuid "c3473de6-e778-5462-bdaf-e07e512b9f0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{4\\sqrt{5}}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353256} {:answer/id #uuid "d924d0f1-1293-5054-8a88-0fb57be38c3a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353454}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186353041} :answer-field/id #uuid "e9848a7e-0635-5dc1-a29b-1065de8cf27f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354214}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "dfa73306-0d2d-5aa8-89e7-e48bb1792f48" :question/math-academy-id "q-86854" :question/problem "$$\nV=\\text{Span}\\{\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}\\},\\,B=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{3\\sqrt{14}}{14} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{14}}{7} \\\\ -\\frac{\\sqrt{14}}{14}\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}a \\\\ b \\\\ c\\end{bmatrix}\\}\n$$\n\nConsider the subspace $V$ and an **orthonormal** basis $B$ of $V,$ given above. Given that $B$ is derived from $V$ using the Gram-Schmidt process, what is the value of $|a|+|b|+|c|?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's denote\n\n$\\,$ ${a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\\,$ and $\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}.$ \n\nWe proceed to find an orthogonal basis using the Gram-Schmidt process, as follows.\n\n**Step 1**: We set ${v}_{1}={a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n**Step 2**: Next, we find ${v}_{2}$, by using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{2} & ={a}_{2}-\\frac{{a}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{v}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the formula for ${v}_{2}$ in our case gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{2} & ={a}_{2}-\\frac{3\\cdot (-3)+0\\cdot 2+5\\cdot (-1)}{(-3)^{2}+{2}^{2}+(-1)^{2}}{v}_{1} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we normalize each vector to get an orthonormal basis:\n\n- ${u}_{1}=\\frac{{v}_{1}}{‖{v}_{1}‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+{2}^{2}+(-1)^{2}}}\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{-3\\sqrt{14}}{14} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{14}}{7} \\\\ -\\frac{\\sqrt{14}}{14}\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n- ${u}_{2}=\\frac{{v}_{2}}{‖{v}_{2}‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{4}^{2}}}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5} \\\\ \\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{5}\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nTherefore, $B=\\{{u}_{1},{u}_{2}\\}=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{-3\\sqrt{14}}{14} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{14}}{7} \\\\ -\\frac{\\sqrt{14}}{14}\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5} \\\\ \\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{5}\\end{bmatrix}\\}$ is an orthonormal basis of $V.$\n\nFinally, $a=0,$ $b=\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5},$ $c=\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{5}$ and  \n\n$$\n|a|+|b|+|c|=|\\,0\\,|+|\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}|+|\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{5}|=\\frac{3\\sqrt{5}}{5}.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "3e0438aa-82a5-54a7-85cc-d1569f51001a"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186502180 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326899 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "47d1854d-6fd6-526c-b759-d1209df8a9d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324552} {:answer/id #uuid "5eb14860-141a-5eac-b5fb-ef7a435dbf1d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324759} {:answer/id #uuid "73d43e73-deae-5a38-b655-86047022d339" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324933} {:answer/id #uuid "aea345a6-603e-546e-ada6-149d72b91b04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325455} {:answer/id #uuid "c3c622cf-8e52-56ac-bc00-2f9457c767f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325654}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186324933} :answer-field/id #uuid "a9ffb187-0527-51f3-b27a-ee8fed1376f3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326526}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "4c9da90f-19cf-5646-82a3-18682358ed1b" :question/math-academy-id "q-41034" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 4 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 7\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}a \\\\ b \\\\ c\\end{bmatrix}\\}\n$$\n\nConsider the subspace $\\text{Col}(A)$ and an orthogonal basis $B$ of $\\text{Col}(A),$ where $A$ and $B$ are given above. Given that $B$ is derived from $\\text{Col}(A)$ using the Gram-Schmidt process, what is the value of $\\frac{b}{a}?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that $\\text{Col}(A)$ is the span of the columns of $A.$  \n\nFirst, let's denote\n\n$\\,$ ${a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\,$ and $\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}.$ \n\nWe proceed to find an orthogonal basis using the Gram-Schmidt process, as follows.\n\n**Step 1**: We set ${v}_{1}={a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n**Step 2**: Next, we find ${v}_{2}$, by using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{2} & ={a}_{2}-\\frac{{a}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{v}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the formula for ${v}_{2}$ in our case gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{2} & ={a}_{2}-\\frac{4\\cdot 3+0\\cdot \\sqrt{3}+7\\cdot 0}{{3}^{2}+(\\sqrt{3})^{2}+{0}^{2}}{v}_{1} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -\\sqrt{3} \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $B=\\{{v}_{1},{v}_{2}\\}=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -\\sqrt{3} \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}\\}$ is an orthogonal basis for $\\text{Col}(A).$\n\nFinally, $a=1,$ $b=-\\sqrt{3},$ and  \n\n$$\n\\frac{b}{a}=\\frac{-\\sqrt{3}}{1}=-\\sqrt{3}.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "560834e6-f0bc-5556-8407-8ecea32f604c" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186502192}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186502192 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134337 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a4ef1ec-81c9-56a1-ae34-cb378d16c96d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324192} {:answer/id #uuid "430eea34-b9a8-5fef-bc38-a0f1f469732d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324511} {:answer/id #uuid "9a68d292-ed71-5037-9830-282f02bf1b9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325285} {:answer/id #uuid "e0be4312-70a5-5ab1-8300-0bd829a9efc3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325935} {:answer/id #uuid "e56aef94-f137-55ff-ac81-7fd165ea233c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325992}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186325992} :answer-field/id #uuid "ccec1e07-b398-56bb-a890-6a479af9136d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326590}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "4388fdfa-5eb8-5165-a253-2f6080a33d4c" :question/math-academy-id "q-41035" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 5 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}a \\\\ b \\\\ c\\end{bmatrix}\\}\n$$\n\nConsider the subspace $\\text{Col}(A)$ and an orthogonal basis $B$ of $\\text{Col}(A),$ where $A$ and $B$ are given above. Given that $B$ is derived from $\\text{Col}(A)$ using the Gram-Schmidt process, what is the value of $\\frac{c}{a}?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that $\\text{Col}(A)$ is the span of the columns of $A.$  \n\nFirst, let's denote\n\n$\\,$ ${a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\\,$ and $\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}.$ \n\nWe proceed to find an orthogonal basis using the Gram-Schmidt process, as follows.\n\n**Step 1**: We set ${v}_{1}={a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n**Step 2**: Next, we find ${v}_{2}$, by using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{2} & ={a}_{2}-\\frac{{a}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{v}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the formula for ${v}_{2}$ in our case gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{2} & ={a}_{2}-\\frac{5\\cdot 4+5\\cdot 4+(-2)\\cdot 2}{{4}^{2}+{4}^{2}+{2}^{2}}{v}_{1} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $B=\\{{v}_{1},{v}_{2}\\}=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}\\}$ is an orthogonal basis for $\\text{Col}(A).$\n\nFinally, $a=1,$ $c=-4,$ and  \n\n$$\n\\frac{c}{a}=\\frac{-4}{1}=-4.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "8acc1726-5d26-585c-9955-88497139998b" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186502175}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186502208 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134310 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "666bb4ea-4b60-5d56-8433-a5bddadd4c14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324825} {:answer/id #uuid "86458e96-03dd-577f-9d42-779768608ee4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325111} {:answer/id #uuid "a169b67a-c0c4-5999-b866-b09a3f19d557" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325340} {:answer/id #uuid "a33a73c3-d148-5248-9684-dc147838d546" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325357} {:answer/id #uuid "eed8102d-4f54-5a30-9a66-7c5e85c93203" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326079}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326079} :answer-field/id #uuid "b17534d5-42e8-5c3f-8bb6-0d2e1eedf4c4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326540}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "84b52cd1-ef6d-51a0-aeac-25f2437c64c6" :question/math-academy-id "q-40739" :question/problem "$$\nV=\\text{Span}\\{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}\\},\\,B=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}a \\\\ b \\\\ c\\end{bmatrix}\\}\n$$\n\nConsider the subspace $V$ and an **orthonormal** basis $B$ of $V,$ given above. Given that $B$ is derived from $V$ using the Gram-Schmidt process, what is the value of $|a|+|b|+|c|?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's denote\n\n$\\,$ ${a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\\,$ and $\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}.$ \n\nWe proceed to find an orthogonal basis using the Gram-Schmidt process, as follows.\n\n**Step 1**: We set ${v}_{1}={a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n**Step 2**: Next, we find ${v}_{2}$, by using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{2} & ={a}_{2}-\\frac{{a}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{v}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the formula for ${v}_{2}$ in our case gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{2} & ={a}_{2}-\\frac{1\\cdot 1+2\\cdot 1+(-3)\\cdot (-1)}{{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}+(-1)^{2}}{v}_{1} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}-2\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we normalize each vector to get an orthonormal basis:\n\n- ${u}_{1}=\\frac{{v}_{1}}{‖{v}_{1}‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}+(-1)^{2}}}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n- ${u}_{2}=\\frac{{v}_{2}}{‖{v}_{2}‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+{0}^{2}+(-1)^{2}}}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ 0 \\\\ -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nTherefore, $B=\\{{u}_{1},{u}_{2}\\}=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ 0 \\\\ -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{bmatrix}\\}$ is an orthonormal basis of $V.$\n\nFinally, $a=-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},$ $b=0,$ $c=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$ and  \n\n$$\n|a|+|b|+|c|=|-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}|+|\\,0\\,|+|\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}|=\\sqrt{2}.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "f6bf6f1f-05a8-52ae-97c6-6d0881baed05" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186502180}}] :activity/title "The Gram-Schmidt Process for Two Vectors" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501459}]}
